// example.greeter — the sample conversation, authored in Yarn Spinner syntax
// (docs/plans/npc-dialogue-yarn.md Phase 1). A .yarn file is one conversation:
// its id is the file stem and its first node is where the conversation starts.
//
// $npc speaks as whichever NPC is playing this conversation. Commands
// (<<give_item>>, <<take_item>>, ...) are the DialogueEffects vocabulary and
// <<if>> takes one DialogueConditions call — the same fixed verbs the in-game
// dialogue editor offers, so Yarn scripts and edited .dialogue.json graphs stay
// interchangeable.

title: hello
---
$npc: New around the station? I can point you somewhere useful.
-> Where's the medbay?
    <<jump medbay>>
-> Here, take this cube off my hands <<if has_item(1)>>
    <<take_item 1>>
    $npc: Huh, a Maguffin Cube. I'll see it gets where it's going.
-> Just passing through
    <<jump farewell>>
===

title: medbay
---
<<give_item 4 1>>
$npc: Two decks down, follow the green stripe. Here, a medkit for the road.
<<jump farewell>>
===

title: farewell
---
$npc: Watch your step out there.
===
